{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-characteristic-classes","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:quantum-characteristic-classes","kind":"definition","title":"Quantum Characteristic Classes","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-recursive-brane-tower","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-yekutieli-lifting-condition"],"examples":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-quantum-characteristic-classes-su2"],"cites":["references/yekutieli2010"],"tags":["yekutieli","obstruction","cohomology","brane-tower"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.QuantumCharacteristicClass","text":"quantum-characteristic-classes.md","leanSource":"quantum-characteristic-classes.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:quantum-characteristic-classes\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be a quantum observable universe. Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\{A_n\\}_{n \\geq 0}</code> be its <a href=\"#def:recursive-brane-tower\" data-at=\"lifting-and-descent/jet-prolongation\">recursive brane tower</a>. Each transition <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A_n \\hookrightarrow A_{n+1}</code> in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{C}</code> defines a central extension of gerbes on the underlying site. The Frobenius–Hopf object <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A_n</code> is an object in a gerbe <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{G}_n</code> banded by the sheaf of units <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{B}</code>. The <a href=\"#prop:jet-prolongation\" data-at=\"lifting-and-descent/jet-prolongation\">jet prolongation</a> produces a central extension:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  1  \\longrightarrow  \\mathcal{B}\n   \\longrightarrow  \\mathfrak{G}_{n+1}\n   \\longrightarrow  \\mathfrak{G}_n\n   \\longrightarrow  1.</code></pre>\n<p>The <strong>quantum characteristic classes</strong> are the cohomology classes</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\kappa_n  \\in  H^2(\\mathcal{S}, \\mathcal{B})</code></pre>\n<p>that obstruct the lifting of objects from <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{G}_n</code> to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{G}_{n+1}</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/quantum-characteristic-classes.md","heading":"Definition","number":"6.4.3","page":"b/def-quantum-characteristic-classes","qa":{"counts":{"pass":83,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":9,"unknown":0,"stale":66},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.QuantumCharacteristicClass","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/quantum-characteristic-classes.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
